---
// macOS builds are ad-hoc signed, so Gatekeeper claims a downloaded .app is
// "damaged". Say so up front: someone who hits that warning with no warning
// assumes the app is broken and leaves. Mirrors the README section.
---

<aside class="note">
  <h3>First launch on macOS</h3>
  <p>
    macOS may say <em>&ldquo;rotreader is damaged and can&rsquo;t be opened&rdquo;</em>. It
    isn&rsquo;t. The builds aren&rsquo;t signed with a paid Apple Developer
    certificate, so macOS blocks them by default. Clear the quarantine flag once,
    after dragging the app to Applications:
  </p>
  <pre><code>xattr -dr com.apple.quarantine /Applications/rotreader.app</code></pre>
</aside>

